<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Feb adjusted jobless rises 5,000 vs Jan.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Feb adjusted jobless rises 5,000 vs Jan.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Feb 97	Jan 97	   Feb 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)		4.672 million   4.658 million	4.270 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		  4.316 million   4.311 million	3.957 million</p>
<p> Change in adj number	+5,000	+145,000	 n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		  12.2 pct    12.2 pct	 11.1 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	  329,380     292,631	  403,000</p>
<p> Vacancies (unadj)	   338,055     297,198	  327,350</p>
<p> Change in numbers in work Dec 96	Nov 96</p>
<p>				  -46,000	-63,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
